#57253
"Cairn Mountain Road - Steep Slope"
"Perched precipitously on the steep grade of a mountainous slope, the road
weaves back and forth along the face, keeping its downward angle to a
reasonable value.  Mostly rock-hard gravel and cobbles, the road appears
capable of standing the test of time.  Large rocks and snow-flocked fir trees
serve as borders along each side of the road.  The mountain way continues
north and downwards for a fair distance, before leveling out to some degree.
Up the mountain to the south, the road reaches a high point and then flattens.
"
