#57294
"Shore - Abandoned Port"
"Sand covers most of the shoreline here, but it gets steadily coarser as it
approaches the water, and finally turns to rocks where it meets the ocean.
Four ancient-looking docks which have mostly fallen apart are lined up in this
vast inlet, intact posts anchored in the rocks along the shore.  It appears
that this was once a busy port; the remains of several warehouses can be made
out just beyond the docks.  Cliffs to the west block passage, their striped
limestone surfaces full of small gaps and ridges.  Against the cliff to the
west are the remains of what must have been a mighty tower.  A sandy, cobbled
road leads into a ravine to the south.
"
