#57298
"Ledge - Hole in the Sea Cliffs"
"This is a limestone ledge, overlooking a vast inlet of the ocean to the east.
A salty haze of sea mist swaths the eastern horizon, and blows pleasantly on
the face of the cliffs.  To the west is a gaping hole in the layered cliff of
limestone, leading into a small passage where only a few feet of tunnel is
visible, and then all that can be seen is a very faint, flickering glow.
Intricate designs are carved into the stone above the entrance, and some
crumbling masonry along the sides of the ledge suggest that this area was once
enclosed in a building.  Small shrubs line the cave's edge, weathered from
life on the edge of the restless sea.  Below to the east a small road leads up
to a sandy beach where decrepit docks can be made out, anchored in the rocks
along the shore.
"
""
