"intricate designs masonry hole flickering glow 1 west"
"The source of the flickering glow in the darkness to the west cannot be
determined from here; only the first few feet of the tunnel are visible.
Highly detailed, swirling designs decorate the stone above and around the
opening in the cliff.  Almost imperceptible highlights of silver can be made
out around some of the patterns.  Masonry along the sides of the ledge to the
north and south includes stone blocks and some rusted metal support beams.
The remains of the tower below, the hanging staircase, and the stonework
around the ledge all suggest that the tower here used to connect directly to
this opening in the cliff.
"
