#57309
"Before a Scintillating Portal"
"The grey slate and limestone walls of this small chamber flicker with many
different colors and shades of light, cast by a shimmering elliptical portal
set on a dais against the western wall.  At the base of the portal is a
shattered glass case with a small stone inside.  Ornate patterns are carved
into the stone around the portal, and silver runes placed in the carving above
and to each side of the portal gleam faintly.  The floor is smooth, worn
limestone, but several fragments of black and white marble tile lying
haphazardly in the corners of the room suggest that it was not always that
way.  Water and then mountains beyond are visible to the east through a gaping
hole in the stone that leads out onto a small stone ledge.
"
"[Kotoktok] portal here, to cult/tomb zone
