#57310
"Shore - Abandoned Port"
"Rocky ramparts block passage to the south and east, their weathered walls
reaching more than fifty feet into the sky.  The shore is sandy below the
cliffs, but becomes steadily more rocky closer to the water.  Four decrepit
docks jut out into the sea, their intact posts anchored amidst the boulders at
the water's edge.  The remains of several large wooden warehouses are nestled
against the cliffs to the south, oriented so that their gates would have faced
the docks.  The beach of coarse sand and stones continues for some distance to
the west, ending where it meets more cliffs.
"
"[Kotoktok] old man here by docks, knows about the portal and how to make it useful
[Kotoktok] story about wizards who delve into spirit world, etc.
"
301465600 0
14 9 0
D3
""
""
0 -1 57294 0 9
E
"decrepit docks posts"
"All that remains of the docks are the posts anchored in the rocks and a few
planks of rotting wood between them.  The spacing of the posts suggests that
the docks used to be wide enough for a two-horse team to pull a wagon out onto
them.
"
E
"remains wooden warehouses"
"The outlines of stone foundations can be seen above the sand, with ancient
wooden columns still anchored at some of the corners.  Waterlogged support
beams and other large wooden elements of the warehouses are piled within the
walls of the foundations.  The rusting hinges of large doors, corroded metal
hooks and several other metal items can be made out amidst the rubbish.
"
